{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/680717-profession-firefighter","id":680717,"title":"Profession: Firefighter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-28T00:26:40-07:00","id":680717,"title":"Profession: Firefighter","content":"So I don't think this one made it out of the old White Wolf forums okay, and since I've been digging around a bit to get back into the groove of things I figure I'll re-post this and collect everyone's thoughts. If this is somehow already on here...well, hopefully one of the mods has a handy delete feature.<br /> <br /> <b>Firefighter</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI\u2019ve seen druggies shootin\u2019 up as their homes burned down around\u2019em. You think you\u2019ll frighten me? I have to go into hell every Goddamn day.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Firefighters aren\u2019t crime fighters (unless they work in the arson division). For the most part, they don\u2019t have the authority to go out and arrest a man, or to carry a firearm on the job. What they do is protect property and save lives. It\u2019s what they\u2019re trained to do. And they\u2019re good at it. It is essential that the same \u201cfight or flight\u201d response a normal person has to danger is rewired in a firefighter\u2019s mind into \u201cfight or fight more\u201d.<br /> <br /> Despite the image of a burly man rushing into a burning building to rescue a life, firefighters are highly educated, learning the physics behind flammable liquids and the myriad types of fires they face. They are required to keep in a semblance of physical shape, and often work out for hours on end to keep up with their demanding jobs.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are many specializations within a fire department depending on the locality. Some departments have companies specializing in water rescue or working aboard fire boats, while others train their crews in high-altitude rescue or wild land firefighting. The skill sets must morph to fit the environment, and for the Vigil that often means a firefighter is able to know exactly how to use a location to their advantage, or ferret out the best way to handle a problem and cover up the evidence (Or at least bribe the arson guys with some scotch and season opener tickets).<br /> <br /> Often, firefighters join the Vigil when they come upon what monsters leave behind. The unquenchable green flames of a magical spell, the victim of a savage werewolf attack, or the still smoking remains of one more extinguished vampire. Rarely do firefighters retire from the Vigil, there's always another in need of saving. Unfortunately for cells, the ten-hour days and nights of many professional fire departments means that on a night where a cell is ready to strike, one of their members might be in the bunk room waiting for a call.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s one benefit a firefighter can bring to bear, it\u2019s their immense sense of camaraderie. A firefighter never leaves a brother firefighter behind, and the same goes when they hunt. Even if a fellow hunter is bitten by a vampire, a firefighter will not leave them behind, and may even do the job of finishing them himself to spare the other hunters the pain.<br /> <br /> In terms of skill sets, firefighters are often by necessity athletic, since a hundred pounds of hoses and water don\u2019t guide themselves. They are also skilled in first aid, able to save a person long enough to get them to the ER. A firefighter must also have a firm grasp of physics, or he could find himself fighting what he thought was an electrical fire, only to be crispered by a leaking gas line, though a skilled driver is invaluable to a company constantly on-call. Finally, a firefighter\u2019s axe and halogen bar make a mean pair of weapons, and a high pressure hose can make quick work of a monster that fears water.<br /> <br /> To many firefighters that join the Vigil, the most obvious organization to join is the Union, since the same neighborhood ethic held by the Union is also shared by many firehouses. However, many firefighters also find a place in the Malleus Maleficarum, since there are still large numbers of Catholic firefighters in the United States. In more rural areas, firefighters may lean towards the Bear Lodge, having grown up hunting alongside running into a flaming structure.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts:</b> High-rise hellraiser, lieutenant-for-life, Chick-magnet hose jockey, skittish probie, boisterous old timer, detached HAZMAT specialist, expert engine driver, fire-obsessed volunteer, fatherly battalion commander, worn-out career man<br /> <br /> <b>Asset Skills:</b> Athletics and Medicine<br /> <br /> <b>Ranks</b><br /> 1 dot: Probie / Volunteer<br /> 2 dots: Firefighter<br /> 3 dots: Engineer / Lieutenant<br /> 4 dots: Captain<br /> 5 dots: Battalion Chief / Fire Marshal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 03-25-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:34:00-07:00","id":682205,"title":"","content":"It's good. I might generalise it to rescue worker (so you might be lifeboat crew, mountain rescue, and so on, as well as firefighter), because I think the character notes and skills would be the same. But it's a good Profession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:42:20-07:00","id":682436,"title":"","content":"A lot of departments actually handle those issues anyway, so when I was writing it I thought it would be redundant. But that proves the point that it isn't common knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T23:32:20-07:00","id":682696,"title":"","content":"Updated the post with small examples of the various positions in many departments and added in some basic concepts in case anyone wants to jump off with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T12:37:07-08:00","id":842682,"title":"","content":"This is super-useful! I don't suppose you have completed stats for a generic firefighter, like they have for police officers in the WoD core rulebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:02:15-08:00","id":842694,"title":"","content":"I think you meant halligan bar, not halogen bar?<br /> <br /> This is awesome! Definitely passes the &quot;Makes me want to play it&quot; test.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:49:12-08:00","id":846402,"title":"","content":"This is great. I was honestly surprised this wasn't a career choice for profession out of the gate. Alright so here's my thoughts, most of the stuff is spot on as far as career goes although I'd change up the part about a firefighter joining the Vigil might be something along the lines of &quot;Often, firefighters join the Vigil when they come upon what monsters leave behind. The unquenchable green flames of a magical spell, the victim of a savage werewolf attack, or the still smoking remains of one more extinguished vampire. Rarely do firefighters retire from the Vigil, there's always another in need of saving.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I think this highlights what makes them different from cops - firefighters are first responders who show up to save lives during a crisis. I think its also worth mentioning the schedules that firefighters keep. Namely that they operate from a Fire House (aptly named this is where the firefighter lives during a shift which can be every other day 24 hours or 2 days 48 hours) when on call they're expected to show up at a moments notice, something that could leave a Cell without a member in a pinch (drama anyone?).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ranks</b><br /> 1 dot: Probie / Volunteer<br /> 2 dots: Firefighter<br /> 3 dots: Engineer / Lieutenant<br /> 4 dots: Captain<br /> 5 dots: Battalion Chief / Fire Marshal<br /> <br /> (This lines the rank structure up with Cop, Chiefs are an entirely bureaucratic and rarely in the field especially in larger cities where there are often district chiefs, on the other hand a Battalion Chief has direct authority over rank-and-file but usually on hand at a fire house)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure I could add a background section if you'd like. My dad is a retired firefighter who spent 3 decades going from Probie to Battalion Chief and even worked a few arson investigations so I had to respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:06:52-07:00","id":853001,"title":"","content":"Edited in the suggestions from SpanishInquisition, if you want to write up a background section I won't stop you man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}